---------------------------- Probes -------------------------

Purpose of Probes
- Make Health Endpoints
    - Liveness probe (health checkup)
    - Readiness probe (when ur probe is going to be ready)
    - startup probe 

################## Implement Liveness Probe ########################

---> vim deployment.yml
--->
kind: Deployment
apiVersion: apps/v1

metadata:
  name: nginx-deployment
  namespace: nginx-dev

spec:
  replicas: 2

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx

  # Pod template
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx

    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:latest
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80

        # Liveness Probe
          livenessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /
              port: 8000
        # Readiness Probe
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /
              port: 8000

          # pod resource quota and limit
          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: 100m
              memory: 128Mi

            limits: # limit means u can max consume 200m CPU and 256Mi memory usage
              cpu: 200m
              memory: 256Mi

          # nginx container path will be mount to one of the volumeMounts
          volumeMounts:
            - mountPath: /var/www/html # nginx html file exist in this location where the nginx data will be stored
              name: nginx-local-pv # this volume name could be something

      volumes:
        - name: nginx-local-pv # this volume name could be something
          persistentVolumeClaim:
            claimName: local-pvc

---